Version 0.8.2 08/January/1996.

Bugfixes and TIME&DATE .


The OOF package contains a Virtual 8086 Monitor (called Virtual Mode
Interface = VMI) and a Forth system running in 32-bit protected mode
(called OOF) with all the source code, some documentation and a few examples.
Although many ANSI FORTH programs will run on the OOF system especially
in the STANDARD mode OOF *IS NOT* an ANSI compliant Forth.
(OOF only provides the majority of the words required by the ANSI Standard.)

